{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ורודף", :translit "v'rodef", :gloss "and pursue"} {:he "וכשלו איש באחיו כמפני חרב ורודף", :translit "v'chash'lu ish b'achiv k'mip'nei cherev v'rodef", :gloss "and they shall stumble a man against his brother as if before the sword and pursue"} {:he "כולו אוהב שוחד ורודף שלמונים", :translit "kulo ohev shochad v'rodef sh'lamim", :gloss "all of it loves bribery and pursues gifts"} {:he "אפרים רועה רוח ורודף קדים", :translit "efra'im ro'eh ruach v'rodef kadim", :gloss "Ephraim feeds on wind and pursues the east"} {:he "וכשלו איש באחיו כמפני חרב ורודף אין", :translit "v'chash'lu ish b'achiv k'mip'nei cherev v'rodef ein", :gloss "and they shall stumble a man against his brother as if before the sword and there is no pursuer"} {:he "עון", :translit "avon", :gloss "iniquity"} {:he "עונם", :translit "avonam", :gloss "their iniquity"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וכשלו איש באחיו כמפני חרב ורודף" "כולו אוהב שוחד ורודף שלמונים" "אפרים רועה רוח ורודף קדים"]} {:kind :masorah, :count 6, :occurrences ["עון" "עונם"]} {:kind :other, :note "Three occurrences of ורודף correspond to three sins: pursuing bribes (Isa 1:23), pursuing the east wind (Hos 12:2), therefore the verse concludes 'and no pursuer' (Lev 26:37)."} {:kind :other, :note "Six occurrences of עון/עונם correspond to six exiles: three by Sennacherib and three by Nebuchadnezzar."}], :frame {:text "The two other occurrences of ורודף come from Isaiah 1:23, 'כולו אוהב שוחד ורודף שלמונים' (every one loves bribes and pursues rewards), and Hosea 12:2, 'אפרים רועה רוח ורודף קדים' (Ephraim feeds on wind and pursues the east wind). These verses describe the northern kingdom's corruption and alliance with Assyria ('קדים' = the east, i.e., Assyria, per Rashi on Hosea 12:2). The closing phrase 'ורודף אין' means they pursued sin, so there will be 'no pursuer' left — the pursuers themselves collapse. Sennacherib's deportations of northern Israelite territories are described in II Kings 17–18, and Nebuchadnezzar's deportations of Judah in II Kings 24–25 and Jeremiah 52.", :sources ["Isaiah 1:23" "Hosea 12:2" "Rashi on Hosea 12:2" "Leviticus 26:37" "II Kings 17" "II Kings 18" "II Kings 24" "II Kings 25" "Jeremiah 52"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["וכשלו איש באחיו כמפני חרב ורודף" "כולו אוהב שוחד ורודף שלמונים" "אפרים רועה רוח ורודף קדים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וכשלו איש באחיו כמפני חרב ורודף", :refs ["Leviticus 26:37"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "כולו אוהב שוחד ורודף שלמונים", :refs ["Isaiah 1:23"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "אפרים רועה רוח ורודף קדים", :refs ["Hosea 12:2"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 6, :occurrences ["עון" "עונם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "עון", :refs ["Genesis 15:16" "Genesis 44:16" "Exodus 20:5" "Exodus 28:38" "Exodus 28:43" "Exodus 34:7" "Leviticus 10:17" "Leviticus 22:16"], :n 65, :lens :exact} {:phrase "עונם", :refs ["Leviticus 20:19" "Leviticus 26:40" "Leviticus 26:41" "Leviticus 26:43" "Numbers 18:23" "Isaiah 13:11" "Jeremiah 14:10" "Jeremiah 16:17"], :n 26, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Three occurrences of ורודף correspond to three sins: pursuing bribes (Isa 1:23), pursuing the east wind (Hos 12:2), therefore the verse concludes 'and no pursuer' (Lev 26:37).", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Six occurrences of עון/עונם correspond to six exiles: three by Sennacherib and three by Nebuchadnezzar.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:24.558408919Z", :model "glm-5.2"}